d focus; mentioned claims and retained prerequisites may extend beyond these goals."},"bundle":{"bundle_id":"qaoa-sk-public-intake","bundle_version":"0.1.0","publication":"local_only","manifest_sha256":"79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb","manifest_ref":"sha256:79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb/manifest.json","graph_sha256":"c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97","graph_ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/graph.json","markdown_sha256":"9e0f6d255eb0a116c513a0c11e94d28559f0a429ef365c3137bb4ff3b6a061d6","markdown_ref":"sha256:9e0f6d255eb0a116c513a0c11e94d28559f0a429ef365c3137bb4ff3b6a061d6/papers/long.md","mapping_sha256":"7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853","mapping_ref":"sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json"},"coverage":{"mapped_content_bytes":235139,"marker_bytes":3192,"unmapped_bytes":26143,"source_bytes_opened":false,"receipt_bytes_opened":false,"per_root_dependency_completeness":"unknown","heading_syntax":"ATX headings only; Setext and HTML headings are not parsed","scope":"Mapped passages are correspondences, not sentence-level formal support. Section-passage overlaps are document structure, not claim or proof implications. Unmapped text and passages omitted by the selector remain in the validated paper. Graph records outside the selected prerequisite closure remain in the bundle and are not asserted absent. Argument links combine recorded Lean references, curated support, formalization correspondence and explicit assumptions; their SCCs describe only that mixed recorded reachability. Reading order and platform decomposition are separate."}},"passages":[{"ref":"sha256:9e0f6d255eb0a116c513a0c11e94d28559f0a429ef365c3137bb4ff3b6a061d6/papers/long.md/sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json/passages/qaoa-finite-size","anchor":"qaoa-finite-size","selected":true,"text":"\n\n<a id=\"finite-size-comparison\"></a>\n\n### 11.5 A later finite-size estimate and its limited depth consequence\n\nA separate, later source gives a quantitative comparison with the\nfixed-angle limit. Boulebnane, Khan, Subrahmanya, Herman, Farhi,\nVillalonga and Shaydulin, [arXiv:2609.40309v1, Corollary S3.1,\npp. 46–47][decoupling], use the ordered-tuple Gaussian mixed-spin cost\nwith covariance polynomial $\\xi(t)=\\sum_q c_q^2t^q$ of finite degree.\nLet $\\Gamma>0$ bound every cost angle in a depth-$p$ word. Choose\n$x>0$ bounding $\\xi(2),\\xi'(1),\\xi''(33)$, with\n$\\Gamma^2p^2x\\ge1$. No bound on the mixer angles is needed. Set\n$$\nB_p=256p^4(2e\\Gamma^2p^2x)^p,\\qquad\nE_p=70\\Gamma^2p^2x+p\\log2,\\qquad\nR_p=(2E_p/\\log2)^{2p}.\n$$\nFor\n$$\n0<\\varepsilon\\le4\\Gamma px\n \\min\\{e^{-1/2},2^{-(8p^2+3)/100}\\},\n$$\nthe source asserts $|\\nu_n-\\nu_\\infty|\\le\\varepsilon$ whenever\n$$\nn\\ge T_p:=\\max\\left\\{\n2^{8p^2+3}B_p\n \\left(\\frac{2^{\\deg\\xi+4}\\Gamma^2p^2x^2}{\\varepsilon^2}\\right)^{R_p}\n \\left[2\\log_2\\frac{4\\Gamma px}{\\varepsilon}+\\deg\\xi\\right]^2,\n\\frac{16\\Gamma px}{\\varepsilon}\\right\\}.\n$$\nHere $\\nu_n$ is the disorder-averaged energy per spin. The estimate\napplies to each near-optimal word from §8.6 separately. Given $\\zeta>0$,\nchoose a finite word $W_\\zeta$ with\n$\\nu_\\infty(W_\\zeta)\\ge P_*-\\zeta/2$. Its depth $p_\\zeta$ and cost\nangles are finite; pad by a zero layer if needed and take\n$\\Gamma_\\zeta=\\max\\{1,\\max_j|\\theta_j(W_\\zeta)|\\}$. Choose a positive\n$\\varepsilon_\\zeta\\le\\zeta/2$ satisfying the displayed small-error\ncondition. With these fixed parameters, the threshold gives\n$$\n\\nu_n(W_\\zeta)\\ge P_*-\\zeta\\qquad(n\\ge T_{p_\\zeta}).\n$$\nThe threshold is explicit in the chosen word and error. The existential\nconstruction supplies no quantitative bounds for $p_\\zeta$ or\n$\\Gamma_\\zeta$ as $\\zeta\\downarrow0$, so it does not yield a bound in\naccuracy alone. A common angle bound is needed for the uniform\ngrowing-depth consequence below, not for this fixed-word application.\n\nFor SK take $c_2=1/\\sqrt2$. Combining the two ordered off-diagonal\ncouplings recovers our standard Gaussian $J_{ij}$; the diagonal adds\nan independent scalar Gaussian of variance $1/2$. That scalar changes\nthe circuit by a global phase and has zero mean, so the expected-energy\ncomparison uses the same normalization. A fixed\n$x\\ge\\max\\{2,\\Gamma^{-2}\\}$ satisfies the above bounds for every\n$p\\ge1$.\n\nFor fixed mixture, $\\Gamma$ and $x$, put $\\varepsilon_p=e^{-p^2}$.\nThe small-error condition holds eventually, and direct logarithms give\n$$\n\\log R_p=4p\\log p+O(p),\\qquad\n\\log\\log T_p=4p\\log p+O(p+\\log p).\n$$\nConsequently, for any deterministic sequence of words $W_n$ with\ndepths $p(n)\\to\\infty$, one common cost-angle bound $\\Gamma$,\nand $p(n)\\log p(n)=o(\\log\\log n)$, the displayed hypotheses hold\nand $|\\nu_n(W_n)-\\nu_\\infty(W_n)|\\le e^{-p(n)^2}$ eventually.\nThis is a uniform comparison along that specified bounded-angle class.\nIt gives neither an efficient way to find near-optimal angles nor\nconcentration of a quantum measurement in this growing-depth regime.\nThe fixed-word second-moment theorem in §11.2 has separate quantifiers.\n","content_span":{"start_byte":222915,"end_byte":226033,"start_line":4810,"end_line":4880},"block_span":{"start_byte":222882,"end_byte":226067,"start_line":4810,"end_line":4881},"section_ref":"sha256:9e0f6d255eb0a116c513a0c11e94d28559f0a429ef365c3137bb4ff3b6a061d6/papers/long.md/sections/187846","evidence_class":"source_argument","rationale":"Transcribes the fixed-word finite-size threshold at the exact cited edition and distinguishes a bound depending on a chosen near-optimal finite word from the additional common-angle hypothesis for a uniform growing-depth family. No effective accuracy-only depth/angle bound or measurement concentration is inferred.","claim_ids":["circuit.later_finite_size_comparison"],"citation_ids":["authored_bounded_angle_depth_comparison","authored_r8_scalar_finite_maximum_concentration","qaoa_finite_size_corollary","qaoa_main_theorem","scalar-r2-26-cite-parisi-formula"],"assumption_ids":[]}],"correspondence_links":[{"from":"sha256:9e0f6d255eb0a116c513a0c11e94d28559f0a429ef365c3137bb4ff3b6a061d6/papers/long.md/sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json/passages/qaoa-finite-size","to":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/circuit.later_finite_size_comparison","kind":"maps_claim","semantic_class":"passage_correspondence","derived":true,"source_ref":"sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json","source_anchor":"qaoa-finite-size","source_field":"claim_ids"},{"from":"sha256:9e0f6d255eb0a116c513a0c11e94d28559f0a429ef365c3137bb4ff3b6a061d6/papers/long.md/sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json/passages/qaoa-finite-size","to":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/citations/authored_bounded_angle_depth_comparison","kind":"maps_citation","semantic_class":"passage_correspondence","derived":true,"source_ref":"sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json","source_anchor":"qaoa-finite-size","source_field":"citation_ids"},{"from":"sha256:9e0f6d255eb0a116c513a0c11e94d28559f0a429ef365c3137bb4ff3b6a061d6/papers/long.md/sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json/passages/qaoa-finite-size","to":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/citations/authored_r8_scalar_finite_maximum_concentration","kind":"maps_citation","semantic_class":"passage_correspondence","derived":true,"source_ref":"sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/l